  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building capacity to reduce bushmeat consumption and trade in neighboring villages around the Bor Corridor, Southern Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Recipient will build the capacity of ex-poachers to address the illegal bushmeat trade in three villages: Jalle, Pariak, and Padak around the Bor migratory corridor in the Boma-Jonglei landscape in Southern Sudan. Through the project, the recipient will raise awareness amongst consumers and sellers of bushmeat in Southern Sudan, and will train ex-poachers to participate in alternative fish protein production and business to reduce bushmeat hunting in the Bor Corridor.</narrative>
  </description>
